The fix removes the explicit `dma_free_coherent()` calls in the error paths of `rtl8180_init_rx_ring()`, so that the function only returns an error code. In `rtl8180_start()`, the error path now jumps to the `err_free_rings` label, which calls `rtl8180_free_rx_ring()` to free all previously allocated resources (including the ring itself and all skbs with their DMA mappings). Setting `priv->rx_buf[i] = NULL` when DMA mapping fails prevents a double free if the caller later tries to free that entry. This ensures that all memory is properly released on failure.

